<title>RUSSIA: Russian Mosenergo 96 sales rise to 14.4 trln rbls.</title>
<headline>Russian Mosenergo 96 sales rise to 14.4 trln rbls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>						   1996	 1995</p>
<p>    sales (trillion roubles)	    14.40	 9.99</p>
<p>including:</p>
<p>     electricity			    10.00	 6.90</p>
<p>     heating				   3.60	 2.30</p>
<p>    pre-tax profit			   3.90	 3.42</p>
<p>    net profit				 2.80	 2.45</p>
<p>    investment				 2.82	 2.00</p>
<p>output:</p>
<p>    electricity (kilowatt/hour)	 73.10 bln   72.70 bln</p>
<p>    heat (gigacalories)		   82.90 million   80.90 million</p>
<p>    new power capacity (megawatts)   220.0	 150.00</p>
<p>    transformer capacity		 355	 1,346</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are preliminary. Full name OAO Energetiki i Elektrifikatsii Mosenergo. The company's authorised capital is 2.55 trillion roubles. Some 49 percent of its shares belongs to national power grid United Energy Systems (UES). Foreign companies hold 35 percent of shares, including 1.5 percent at Crawford Holding Ltd. Bank of New York is nominal shareholder of 20-25 percent of shares for an ADR programme. Russian companies own 3.6 percent of shares. Private investors hold about 12 percent of shares.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
